 "title": "Возвращение на кухню  (Return to the Kitchen)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max has been sent to wash dishes, and he has taken the order literally. Barinov finds him sitting around and wants to know who suspended him. Here goes.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Макс, ты что здесь прохлаждаешься?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что мне еще делать, шеф?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Меня сегодня отстранили от работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто тебя отстранил? Я?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Виктория Сергеевна сказала сидеть здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "С каких пор ты её слушаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На этой кухне главный только я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она обещала меня уволить, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Увольнять поваров могу только я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А ну марш на кухню!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Там тебя куча чеков дожидается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо, шеф, я бегу!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Стой, куда ты понес сковороду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На рабочее место, шеф!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's take it slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Макс, ты что здесь прохлаждаешься?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, why are you slacking off here?' We can consider this line: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "прохлаждаешься",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'cooling yourself off', from the noun for 'coolness', a relative of 'cold'. You can use it for someone taking it easy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что мне еще делать, шеф?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What else am I to do, chef?' The expression is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "мне",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "еще",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "делать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'what to me still to do'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "делать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'to do', in the dictionary form. It's the question of a worker who has been given no job.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Меня сегодня отстранили от работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I was suspended from work today.' Now let's focus on the phrase: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "отстранили",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'they moved aside', with nobody named: the ending says 'they' without saying who. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "от",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "работы",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'from work'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто тебя отстранил? Я?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who suspended you? Me?' Barinov repeats the verb, now as ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "отстранил",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", with a masculine ending. The pause between 'who' and 'I' is the joke. He cannot bear that anyone else makes decisions in his kitchen.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Виктория Сергеевна сказала сидеть здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Viktoria Sergeyevna told me to sit here.' First name plus father's name, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сергеевна",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is the polite way to name the art director. And ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "сказала",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "сидеть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'said to sit', needs no 'that' between.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "С каких пор ты её слушаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Since when do you listen to her?' The expression is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "С",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "каких",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "пор",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'from which times', for 'since when'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "слушаешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'listen', means 'obey' here, as in English 'listen to your mother'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На этой кухне главный только я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'In this kitchen, only I am the boss!' Let's break down the phrase: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "главный",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'main', is the chunk from 'who is the most important'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "только",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "я",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'only I', puts the stress on him. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "этой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "кухне",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'on this kitchen'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она обещала меня уволить, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She promised to fire me, chef.' Now let's look at this line: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "обещала",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'promised', has a feminine ending, because a woman made the promise. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "уволить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'to fire', gives the term Alisa used when she threatened Lyova. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "меня",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'me'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Увольнять поваров могу только я!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only I can fire cooks!' Let us break down this line: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Увольнять",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'to fire', here is the form for doing it again and again, as a power. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "поваров",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the noun for 'cooks', as the ones being fired. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "могу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'I can'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А ну марш на кухню!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now march to the kitchen!' Now let's break down this line: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ну",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a push, something like 'come on, now'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "марш",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a military 'march'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "на",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "кухню",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'to the kitchen', the same as in Vika's order.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Там тебя куча чеков дожидается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A pile of orders is waiting for you there.' Let us inspect the sentence: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "куча",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'heap', is everyday speech for 'lots'. The order slips are ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "чеков",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'checks'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "дожидается",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'waits until you come', from the verb 'to wait'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо, шеф, я бегу!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you, chef, I am running!' We will look at the speech: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "бегу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'I run', said in the middle of the movement. You can say 'I run' for 'I'm on my way!'. Max is delighted.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Стой, куда ты понес сковороду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait, where are you carrying that pan?' Now let's consider the sentence: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "понес",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'carried', with a prefix for setting off, so Barinov catches him in the act. The noun for pan becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "сковороду",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", as the thing carried. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Стой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'stop'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На рабочее место, шеф!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'To the workstation, chef!' Let us break down the phrase: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "рабочее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "место",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'to the working place'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "рабочее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from the noun for 'work'. Max keeps hold of the pan, and the scene ends. Here it is, all together.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
